OL,3,GNEWSACPS apologises to man after
OL,4,AThetford prison error
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Crown Prosecution Service (CPS) has
OL,7,Fapologised to a man who remained in
OL,8,Fprison despite charges against him
OL,9,Fbeing dropped.
OL,11,FJames Jobson, 62, from Costessey near
OL,12,FNorwich, had been accused of sharing
OL,13,Fdetails of properties housing asylum
OL,14,Fseekers and remanded in custody
OL,15,Ffollowing anti-immigration disorder in
OL,16,FThetford, but Norfolk Police said on
OL,17,FFriday that no further action would be
OL,18,Ftaken.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,377,370,200,160,0,100
